To round to the nearest hundredth, I need to look at the digit in the hundredths place and the digit in the thousandths place.
The number is $1.423$.
The digit in the tenths place is $4$.
The digit in the hundredths place is $2$.
The digit in the thousandths place is $3$.

To round to the nearest hundredth, I look at the digit in the thousandths place.
The digit in the thousandths place is $3$.
Since $3 < 5$, I round down.
So, the digit in the hundredths place remains $2$.
The number rounded to the nearest hundredth is $1.42$.

b) The number is $3.2387$.
